# This CITATION.cff file describes how to cite this software.
# Schema: https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# DRAFT: the author list and contributor roles below should be reviewed by the
# maintainers against the Zenodo record before this file is published.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  open-gira: Open Global Infrastructure Risk/Resilience Analysis
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself (via the
  Zenodo DOI below) and, where relevant, the specific data release you used.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Tom
    family-names: Russell
    affiliation: University of Oxford
  - given-names: Fred
    family-names: Thomas
    affiliation: University of Oxford
    email: fred.thomas@eci.ox.ac.uk
  # Further contributors are listed in the repository history and on the
  # Zenodo record; please add them here as appropriate.
repository-code: 'https://github.com/nismod/open-gira'
url: 'https://nismod.github.io/open-gira'
abstract: >-
  open-gira is an open-source snakemake workflow for analysing environmental
  risks to infrastructure networks using global open data. It builds
  infrastructure networks from OpenStreetMap and other open sources, intersects
  them with hazard data (river and coastal flooding, tropical cyclones,
  landslides), and estimates direct damages and disruption.
license: MIT
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.14537079
    description: The concept DOI for all versions of open-gira.
keywords:
  - infrastructure
  - climate risk
  - natural hazards
  - snakemake
  - open data
  - flooding
  - tropical cyclones
